{
  "format": "OrganizeOS rich-text nodes, version 1",
  "about": "Each case is sanitised rich-text HTML and the `nodes` /v1 sends for it (toRichTextNodes in client/lib/collections/rich-text-nodes.ts). The builder fork copies this file unchanged and tests the RichText component against it. Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-cms-in-the-builder-design.md section 4.7.",
  "limits": {
    "maxDepth": 8,
    "maxNodes": 5000,
    "depth": "Block nesting: top-level blocks are at depth 1, and the blocks of a quote or of a list item are one deeper. A quote or list that would sit at depth 8 becomes a paragraph of its plain text.",
    "count": "Every block and inline counts; the root does not. A tree over 5,000 nodes keeps its first 4,998 in document order (a container left empty by the cut goes), and the text of everything after them becomes one trailing paragraph, so the tree ends at no more than 5,000 nodes.",
    "plainText": "Plain text joins text nodes, puts a space at each line break and block boundary, collapses runs of whitespace to one space and trims."
  },
  "cases": [
